{
  "description": "Front Garden T1 - Sycamore- Undertake a crown reduction of approximately 1.5 metres, selectively reducing the overall crown dimensions back to suitable secondary growth points and appropriate lateral branches whilst maintaining furnishing growth.\rRear Garden T2 - Bay Tree- Undertake a crown reduction of approximately 4 metres in height, together with selective crown reshaping to improve the overall form and proportions of the tree.  \rT3 - Laurel- Prune back the Laurel away from the adjoining property to establish approximately 1 metre of clearance from the building.  \rT4 - Lime Tree- Undertake repollarding of the lime tree, reducing the crown back to its previously established pollard points. The works will maintain the existing pollarding management regime, retaining the established pollard framework and furnishing growth. \rT5 - Silver Birch - Closest to Property Undertake a selective crown reduction to the Silver Birch, reducing the overall height by approximately 1 metre and the lateral crown spread by up to 0.5 metres on the side closest to the property. Pruning cuts will be made back to suitable growth points  maintaining the natural form of the tree. \rAs an Arboricultural Approved contractor (#AC2626), all works will be undertaken in accordance with BS 39982010 - Tree Work - Recommendations. Reason for work: General tree maintenance",
